From: rawaha-e <219735494+rawaha-e@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 10:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] modules: don't reset LDFLAGS

"LDFLAGS =" in src/modules/Makefile.am throws away the LDFLAGS given to
configure, so the output modules and libspeechd_module are linked
without them (no GNU_HASH, no -Wl,-O1, no relro...).

Only the line removal from the upstream commit is backported here; the
rest of that commit adds the piper module.

Upstream-Status: Backport [https://github.com/brailcom/speechd/commit/6511762e595e35c026c712ca8857053b29726647]
Signed-off-by: rawaha-e <219735494+rawaha-e@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/src/modules/Makefile.am
+++ b/src/modules/Makefile.am
@@ -27,7 +27,6 @@
 CLEANFILES = dummy-message.wav
 
 inc_local = -I$(top_srcdir)/include -I$(top_srcdir)/src/common
-LDFLAGS =
 
 if DARWIN_HOST
 LDFLAGS += -Wl,-U,_module_speak -Wl,-U,_module_speak_sync
